<code>assert 0 <= index && index < this.size() && role != null => this.get(index) == \old(this.get(index));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index < this.size() && role != null => this.get(index) == \old(this.get(index));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index < this.size() && role != null => \result == \old(this.get(index));</code>

However, since the `set` method does not return any value (`void`), we cannot use `\result`. Instead, we need to check that the value at the given index is updated correctly. Here is the corrected assert statement:

<code>assert 0 <= index && index < this.size() && role != null => this.get(index) == role;</code>
--------------------
